1
00:00:09,134 --> 00:00:11,094
This is the pre-boarding announcement

2
00:00:11,178 --> 00:00:15,682
for Lusit Airways flight
LLT154 to Marrakech.

3
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:18,310
We are now inviting those
classified as small children...

4
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:19,603
Come on. Where are you?

5
00:00:23,774 --> 00:00:24,985
Please have your boarding pass

6
00:00:24,986 --> 00:00:27,528
and identification ready. Thank you.

7
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:29,988
- ETA?
- Less than a minute.

8
00:00:40,874 --> 00:00:42,876
- Has there been a handover?
- Negative.

9
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:49,007
Eyes on Dogs.

10
00:00:57,432 --> 00:01:00,352
Why is he airside? Intel
said target was inbound.

11
00:01:00,352 --> 00:01:01,895
He made visual contact, ma'am.

12
00:01:01,979 --> 00:01:03,105
Reconfirm.

13
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:04,940
Second Desk requests
we reconfirm visual.

14
00:01:05,022 --> 00:01:08,694
You're looking for an Asian male,
20s, backpack, blue shirt, white tee.

15
00:01:08,694 --> 00:01:12,072
Yes, confirmed, and I
have Dogs on standing by.

16
00:01:17,661 --> 00:01:18,829
Shit.

17
00:01:18,829 --> 00:01:21,039
Lost visual. Possible handover.

18
00:01:21,123 --> 00:01:22,624
What does he mean "possible handover"?

19
00:01:22,708 --> 00:01:24,835
- Cartwright, clarify.
- Did you catch anything on CCTV?

20
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:29,173
Negative, that's what you're
there for. Repeat, clarify.

21
00:01:29,173 --> 00:01:30,883
He has a visual. Did he
see a handover or not?

22
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:32,843
Lost visual momentarily.

23
00:01:32,843 --> 00:01:34,720
Repeat, possible handover.

24
00:01:35,304 --> 00:01:37,389
- Come on. Get out of the way.
- Blocked by the cleaner.

25
00:01:37,890 --> 00:01:40,392
Lusit Airways are pleased
to announce boarding

26
00:01:40,392 --> 00:01:43,437
for flight LLT154 to Marrakech.

27
00:01:43,437 --> 00:01:46,690
We would like to invite families
and those requiring assistance

28
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:48,525
- to come forward first.
- Move, move, move.

29
00:01:48,609 --> 00:01:51,236
Please have your passports
and boarding card ready.

30
00:01:52,905 --> 00:01:54,740
Okay, have full visual on target again,

31
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:56,992
but something has definitely
gone in or out of that backpack.

32
00:01:56,992 --> 00:01:58,076
Tell him to hold.

33
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:00,495
Cartwright, hold your
position. Do not intercept.

34
00:02:02,206 --> 00:02:05,083
- Target is on the move.
- We have eyes on target. Hold.

35
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:06,168
Ma'am?

36
00:02:07,261 --> 00:02:08,295
Hold your position, Cartwright.

37
00:02:08,296 --> 00:02:10,797
Hold your position. We are assessing.

38
00:02:10,881 --> 00:02:13,091
Target is joining the
queue to board. Standing by.

39
00:02:13,175 --> 00:02:14,593
Keep the channel clear, please.

40
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:17,471
Come on.

41
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:20,307
Second Desk says, "Do not intercept."

42
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:25,020
Come on, come on, come on, come on.

43
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:30,817
- Push the button.
- Dogs are standing by, ma'am.

44
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:35,572
At least he's heading downstairs.
There's 300 bodies up there.

45
00:02:35,656 --> 00:02:37,866
Yes, but he's headed to
a plane loaded with fuel.

46
00:02:38,534 --> 00:02:40,953
First passengers are
on the tarmac, ma'am.

47
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:47,793
- Authorize.
- Apprehend suspect.

48
00:02:47,793 --> 00:02:48,961
Dogs, go.

49
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,548
Move!

50
00:02:54,842 --> 00:02:56,969
- Out of the way!
- Move!

51
00:02:59,096 --> 00:03:00,556
- Down, down, down!
- What the fuck?

52
00:03:00,556 --> 00:03:02,516
Get the fuck off me!

53
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:05,352
Disperse if you can. Keep calm.

54
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:07,729
- Get back!
- Get off me!

55
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:09,481
- What the fuck?
- Relax!

56
00:03:09,565 --> 00:03:11,149
- What are you doing?
- No trigger.

57
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:12,901
- This is fucking harassment!
- No wires here.

58
00:03:12,985 --> 00:03:14,695
- Clear.
- Bag.

59
00:03:15,988 --> 00:03:17,948
- Get off! Get off me.
- Over.

60
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:24,621
Somebody film this! Fuck!

61
00:03:24,705 --> 00:03:26,957
- Get off me! Nothing on me!
- Stop moving!

62
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:32,629
He's clean.

63
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:35,299
Repeat. Repeat!

64
00:03:35,299 --> 00:03:37,801
He's clean. There's no
device, no weapon. Nothing.

65
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:39,428
- Ma'am?
- He has the wrong suspect,

66
00:03:39,428 --> 00:03:41,597
or we have the wrong intel, and
we don't have the wrong intel.

67
00:03:41,597 --> 00:03:43,974
- Ma'am, he reconfirmed visual.
- Reconfirm again.

68
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:45,809
Cartwright, confirm suspect description.

69
00:03:45,893 --> 00:03:49,521
Asian male, 20s, backpack,
blue shirt, white tee.

70
00:03:49,605 --> 00:03:51,106
I said, "white shirt, blue tee."

71
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:53,525
You...

72
00:03:53,609 --> 00:03:56,737
No, no, no, no, you said... you
said, "blue shirt, white tee."

73
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:58,363
Webb.

74
00:04:00,449 --> 00:04:02,367
Shit. Put it on the main screen.

75
00:04:02,451 --> 00:04:04,786
White shirt, blue tee.
Suspect is inbound.

76
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:06,914
Inbound, headed to
immigration, main terminal.

77
00:04:06,914 --> 00:04:08,332
Stand Cartwright down. He's done.

78
00:04:08,332 --> 00:04:10,709
Second Desk says stand down, Cartwright.

79
00:04:13,337 --> 00:04:14,630
Oh, shit.

80
00:04:16,005 --> 00:04:17,966
- Stand him down.
- Cartwright, where are you going?

81
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:19,843
You tailed the wrong
suspect. You're stood down.

82
00:04:19,927 --> 00:04:21,678
Get me CCTV on that escalator now.

83
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:28,852
- Should we have immigration hold him up?
- Not with a bomb on his back.

84
00:04:28,936 --> 00:04:30,479
- Get SO15 on standby.
- Ma'am.

85
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:32,231
SO15, standby.

86
00:04:38,237 --> 00:04:40,030
- He'll be through in two minutes.
- Duffy, where are your Dogs?

87
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:41,532
Still airside with Cartwright's suspect.

88
00:04:41,532 --> 00:04:44,117
Jesus Christ! If you
can't get your guys there,

89
00:04:44,201 --> 00:04:45,911
get SO15 on the ground now.

90
00:04:45,911 --> 00:04:47,496
We got something behind immigration?

91
00:04:47,496 --> 00:04:48,539
Excuse me.

92
00:04:48,539 --> 00:04:50,666
Hey! Hey!

93
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:53,627
- How long?
- Three minutes.

94
00:04:53,627 --> 00:04:54,878
He's through.

95
00:05:00,884 --> 00:05:02,594
There. He's headed to baggage reclaim.

96
00:05:02,678 --> 00:05:04,888
Stay on him. I need eyes at
the end of that concourse.

97
00:05:04,972 --> 00:05:06,807
- Yep. Coming up now.
- Head to the carousel.

98
00:05:11,562 --> 00:05:12,980
He's Headed to baggage reclaim.

99
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:14,690
Give me cameras at the
end of baggage reclaim.

100
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:16,191
I want eyes there.

101
00:05:28,912 --> 00:05:30,455
Not a Dog in sight.

102
00:05:30,539 --> 00:05:31,623
Duffy, those are your guys?

103
00:05:31,707 --> 00:05:33,208
No. No, ma'am. They're en route.

104
00:05:33,292 --> 00:05:35,335
Duffy, surely we've got transport
police on that concourse.

105
00:05:35,419 --> 00:05:37,171
Waiting. Inbound, two minutes.

106
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:42,134
Thank you!

107
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,305
He's not waiting for luggage.

108
00:05:46,305 --> 00:05:48,348
What? He's walking straight out.

109
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,235
Get out of the way! Move!

110
00:06:00,319 --> 00:06:03,071
Move, move, move, move!

111
00:06:04,656 --> 00:06:05,782
Sorry.

112
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,452
- Whoa, whoa!
- I'm service, I'm service.

113
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:10,871
I'm service! Move now!

114
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:17,461
- I need an image. Why is it dark in there?
- There's no cameras, ma'am.

115
00:06:17,461 --> 00:06:19,171
- I want eyes now!
- Confirm with Stansted.

116
00:06:19,171 --> 00:06:21,924
Dogs, intercept! Suspect's
now landside. Where are you?

117
00:06:27,971 --> 00:06:29,180
- There.
- He swapped backpacks.

118
00:06:29,181 --> 00:06:30,181
That's the handover.

119
00:06:30,849 --> 00:06:31,849
Smash the glass.

120
00:06:33,352 --> 00:06:35,646
This is an emergency. Please evacuate.

121
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:42,152
Ladies and gentlemen, please
evacuation the terminal!

122
00:06:42,236 --> 00:06:43,820
Evacuate the terminal all the way...

123
00:06:43,904 --> 00:06:45,989
- ... this exit. This exit.
- Work out the safe areas.

124
00:06:46,073 --> 00:06:47,491
Keep them safe. Don't let anyone pass.

125
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,919
This way please. Ladies and
gentlemen, this way. Quick as you can.

126
00:07:06,802 --> 00:07:07,845
Move, move, move, move!

127
00:07:10,556 --> 00:07:11,640
Move!

128
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:22,568
Move! Aside!

129
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:25,195
Move! Out of the way! Now!

130
00:07:26,905 --> 00:07:28,699
He's headed for the Stansted Express.

131
00:07:31,285 --> 00:07:32,744
Get out of the way!

132
00:07:35,205 --> 00:07:37,040
Move! Get to the side.

133
00:07:37,124 --> 00:07:38,292
Come on!

134
00:07:40,961 --> 00:07:42,421
Get it cleared. Full evacuation.

135
00:07:42,421 --> 00:07:44,089
Evacuate the entire train station.

136
00:07:44,173 --> 00:07:46,466
I want any trains coming
into Stansted halted.

137
00:07:46,550 --> 00:07:48,635
Any trains that are in-bound,
I need to know about it.

138
00:07:48,719 --> 00:07:50,137
Move, move, move!

139
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:57,811
Move, move, move!

140
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,773
Move, move, move!

141
00:08:02,441 --> 00:08:04,985
- Move, move, move, move, move!
- This way!

142
00:08:06,028 --> 00:08:07,779
Keep moving, guys. Come on.

143
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:11,033
Place is closed! Stop! Stop!

144
00:08:11,033 --> 00:08:13,410
What are you doing?

145
00:08:24,963 --> 00:08:30,511
Stop! No! Step away now!
Step away! Don't do it!

146
00:11:28,772 --> 00:11:29,773
No?

147
00:11:30,566 --> 00:11:31,859
Yeah? Great!

148
00:11:49,376 --> 00:11:50,669
Standish.

149
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:04,266
- Are you all in?
- All except River and Sid.

150
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:07,227
Yeah, well, the last
one in can clean my lav.

151
00:12:10,564 --> 00:12:13,192
I thought spooks were
supposed to be stealthy.

152
00:12:17,779 --> 00:12:21,116
Another day dawns on
MI-Fucking Useless.

153
00:12:56,652 --> 00:12:57,986
Morning, Max.

154
00:12:58,070 --> 00:13:00,030
The usual, Mr. Hobden?

155
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:02,115
Yes, Max. The usual.

156
00:13:08,914 --> 00:13:10,499
His name isn't Max.

157
00:13:11,792 --> 00:13:13,710
Well, it says "Max" on
the front of the shop.

158
00:13:13,794 --> 00:13:17,089
Yeah, but I heard the staff call
him Theo, short for Theodosios.

159
00:13:18,131 --> 00:13:19,800
I'll stick with "Max." Shorter.

160
00:13:24,012 --> 00:13:25,305
There you go.

161
00:13:25,389 --> 00:13:27,224
Thank you, Max.

162
00:13:48,954 --> 00:13:50,205
What are you looking for?

163
00:13:52,291 --> 00:13:54,334
A reason not to blow my brains out.

164
00:13:57,754 --> 00:13:59,673
He hasn't told me yet
what I'm looking for.

165
00:13:59,673 --> 00:14:01,842
Dumping the rubbish
this side of the room.

166
00:14:01,842 --> 00:14:04,303
Do you think Sid will find
this as amusing as you do?

167
00:14:11,476 --> 00:14:12,853
- Hello, Catherine.
- Morning.

168
00:14:12,853 --> 00:14:13,937
Morning.

169
00:14:16,231 --> 00:14:18,775
Bradford driving license applications,

170
00:14:18,859 --> 00:14:22,529
addresses, council tax
records. Cross-check.

171
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:24,573
Well, these are from 2005.

172
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:27,993
The lending list from Luton
libraries in the last year.

173
00:14:27,993 --> 00:14:29,453
At least yours is topical.

174
00:14:29,453 --> 00:14:31,705
Flag any borrowing that
suggests money laundering.

175
00:14:31,705 --> 00:14:34,374
Really? Someone looking
that up in the library

176
00:14:34,458 --> 00:14:36,376
probably doesn't have
that much money to launder.

177
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,587
Parking tickets from the Euston area.

178
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:42,799
From the '90s?

179
00:14:42,883 --> 00:14:44,343
No stone unturned, eh?

180
00:14:44,343 --> 00:14:45,469
Oh, Catherine!

181
00:14:45,469 --> 00:14:48,555
Catherine, before you go,
these two stick-in-the-muds

182
00:14:48,639 --> 00:14:51,683
are giving my idea of a pub
quiz team a big thumbs down.

183
00:14:51,767 --> 00:14:53,519
Actually, I gave it a fat middle finger.

184
00:14:53,519 --> 00:14:57,147
Come on, guys! What about
team spirit? Catherine?

185
00:14:57,231 --> 00:14:58,232
No.

186
00:14:58,232 --> 00:15:01,527
- "No," as in "Ask me later," or... or no...
- As in, "no."

187
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:06,365
Tough nut to crack, that
Catherine, but I'll get there.

188
00:15:06,365 --> 00:15:08,909
- Forget it. She never lightens up.
- Would you?

189
00:15:08,909 --> 00:15:11,161
If I was Lamb's lackey, no.

190
00:15:11,245 --> 00:15:14,248
No, I meant what happened
before. Before she came here.

191
00:15:14,248 --> 00:15:16,667
Yeah, well, I... I wish
Lamb would go that way.

192
00:15:21,588 --> 00:15:24,883
Is today the day you finally give
me something remotely challenging?

193
00:15:25,592 --> 00:15:28,637
Flight inquiries to Syria
from the previous decade.

194
00:15:29,179 --> 00:15:31,014
No, it isn't.

195
00:15:31,098 --> 00:15:32,683
Well, I'll set up an algorithm for that

196
00:15:32,683 --> 00:15:35,853
and treat the remaining nine
hours of the day as my own time.

197
00:15:36,979 --> 00:15:39,523
Jed? Transport police are asking

198
00:15:39,523 --> 00:15:42,401
if you can stop scaring
people away from that bus stop.

199
00:15:43,277 --> 00:15:46,572
- They could be watching us.
- Or they could be waiting for a bus.

200
00:15:47,322 --> 00:15:49,575
Also, Lamb says there's a new hire

201
00:15:49,575 --> 00:15:51,451
- at the Chinese down...
- Oh, fuck me!

202
00:15:51,535 --> 00:15:53,078
- And he'd like...
- I know, I know.

203
00:15:53,078 --> 00:15:54,413
Interview and background.

204
00:15:54,413 --> 00:15:55,831
And if he happens to be undocumented,

205
00:15:55,832 --> 00:15:57,916
it's five free meals
to look the other way.

206
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,209
Man.

207
00:16:00,043 --> 00:16:02,588
No, I've been keeping
me eyes on the water.

208
00:16:02,588 --> 00:16:04,298
I'm just waiting for a fin to surface,

209
00:16:04,298 --> 00:16:09,428
but I need you to guarantee
me 2,000 words once it breaks.

210
00:16:09,428 --> 00:16:11,263
It's like your Watergate.

211
00:16:12,931 --> 00:16:15,225
You know what? I can't
tell you now because it...

212
00:16:23,775 --> 00:16:27,279
Sorry, um, the reason
I interrupted before

213
00:16:27,279 --> 00:16:29,695
is because I spent a
year studying in Greece

214
00:16:29,696 --> 00:16:31,533
and the name caught my ear.

215
00:16:32,034 --> 00:16:34,203
Was a great country a
couple of thousand years ago.

216
00:16:34,203 --> 00:16:35,954
Yeah.

217
00:16:36,038 --> 00:16:37,765
And I'm interrupting
now because I was hoping

218
00:16:37,766 --> 00:16:39,500
I could borrow your Times.

219
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,837
Fine.

220
00:16:43,921 --> 00:16:45,380
Thank you.

221
00:16:45,464 --> 00:16:47,090
Oh, what...

222
00:16:47,174 --> 00:16:48,800
- Oh, my God. I am so...
- Oh, shit.

223
00:16:48,884 --> 00:16:50,969
- I am so sorry. I'm so sorry. Sorry.
- Oh, shit.

224
00:16:51,637 --> 00:16:56,016
Can I please have some towels? Okay.
Can I just have some serviettes?

225
00:16:56,016 --> 00:16:58,185
No, I need more serviettes.

226
00:16:58,185 --> 00:17:00,771
- God, I'm so, um, um...
- Here. Here.

227
00:17:00,771 --> 00:17:02,481
Yeah, napkins. Can we get some more?

228
00:17:02,481 --> 00:17:03,690
- Oh!
- Thank you.

229
00:17:03,774 --> 00:17:07,277
Max, this is not enough. Have you...
Have you got any more serviettes?

230
00:17:07,361 --> 00:17:09,570
- Max, pass me that.
- Take this. Take this.

231
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:13,742
- Just leave it. Excuse me.
- I'm so, so clumsy.

232
00:17:13,742 --> 00:17:16,369
- Would you leave it?
- No, I feel so bad. Is your laptop okay?

233
00:17:16,453 --> 00:17:18,413
It's okay. Let me clean it up now.

234
00:17:18,955 --> 00:17:19,998
Fuck!

235
00:17:20,582 --> 00:17:22,291
Fucking...

236
00:17:39,685 --> 00:17:40,811
You thumped?

237
00:17:42,437 --> 00:17:43,647
Did you find anything?

238
00:17:45,190 --> 00:17:46,608
I don't know what I'm looking for.

239
00:17:46,692 --> 00:17:50,779
Yeah, uh, the remnants of
a once-promising career.

240
00:17:52,948 --> 00:17:56,451
Are we actually acting on any
intel, or are we just fishing?

241
00:17:56,535 --> 00:17:58,829
Yeah, but now, you don't
get to ask questions.

242
00:17:59,329 --> 00:18:02,291
That's for spies who
haven't shat the bed.

243
00:18:02,875 --> 00:18:06,420
So, what did you find?
Any old notebooks?

244
00:18:07,671 --> 00:18:10,132
Uh, the cardboard backing
of one, but no pages.

245
00:18:10,132 --> 00:18:11,592
Evidence of drug use?

246
00:18:11,592 --> 00:18:13,635
Empty box of paracetamol, yeah.

247
00:18:13,719 --> 00:18:15,179
Empty booze bottles?

248
00:18:15,179 --> 00:18:17,431
In his recycling bin, I imagine.

249
00:18:17,431 --> 00:18:19,433
