00:34:35,576 --> 00:34:37,995
Absolutely not. That'd
be a full-time job.

493
00:34:37,995 --> 00:34:41,331
All right. You're here after
hours. What's your excuse?

494
00:34:41,415 --> 00:34:43,000
I left my phone charger.

495
00:34:43,708 --> 00:34:45,918
A phone charger. You came all
the way back for a phone charger?

496
00:34:46,003 --> 00:34:48,380
- I was having drinks nearby.
- Well, thanks for the invite.

497
00:34:49,422 --> 00:34:51,425
I've invited you before
and you turned me down.

498
00:34:51,507 --> 00:34:52,509
- What? No...
- Once bitten...

499
00:34:52,509 --> 00:34:53,886
- No, you haven't.
- Yes, I have.

500
00:34:53,886 --> 00:34:55,179
No. It...

501
00:34:57,139 --> 00:34:58,432
Fucking hell.

502
00:34:58,432 --> 00:35:02,603
If people are happy to spend time
in this building after 5:00 p.m.,

503
00:35:03,520 --> 00:35:05,981
then I'm not really doing my job.

504
00:35:07,983 --> 00:35:09,401
Uh, I left my phone charger.

505
00:35:09,943 --> 00:35:11,987
I was gonna clean up the rubbish. Sorry.

506
00:35:14,072 --> 00:35:15,115
Fuck off.

507
00:35:16,241 --> 00:35:19,578
"Fuck off" as in go home, or "fuck
off" as in you don't believe us?

508
00:35:20,078 --> 00:35:21,820
At the end of the working day,

509
00:35:21,821 --> 00:35:25,083
your pitiful, miserable
time is your own.

510
00:35:26,126 --> 00:35:32,126
But if I find out you are indulging
in extracurricular activities

511
00:35:32,466 --> 00:35:36,970
that could upset the equilibrium
of this blessed sanctuary,

512
00:35:38,138 --> 00:35:42,726
then I will make it so that you
wish you were in a Siberian gulag.

513
00:36:09,795 --> 00:36:11,171
Mmm. Twice in one day.

514
00:36:11,755 --> 00:36:14,800
That girl earlier. The
one who spilled my coffee.

515
00:36:14,800 --> 00:36:17,302
Did she leave soon after me?

516
00:36:17,386 --> 00:36:20,264
I can't remember. I think so.

517
00:36:21,306 --> 00:36:23,475
Well, has she been in here before?

518
00:36:23,559 --> 00:36:24,852
A few times recently.

519
00:36:26,270 --> 00:36:30,524
Oh, yeah. Well, if she comes in again...

520
00:36:33,569 --> 00:36:34,778
give me a call.

521
00:36:35,487 --> 00:36:36,572
- Yeah?
- Sure.

522
00:36:48,625 --> 00:36:49,751
Dirty old man.

523
00:37:23,202 --> 00:37:25,100
Yeah, looking back I probably

524
00:37:25,101 --> 00:37:27,331
already had a drinking problem.

525
00:37:27,331 --> 00:37:33,331
But, um, when my dad died, I
just got really, really lost.

526
00:37:33,504 --> 00:37:36,965
He was 56. Aneurysm. Gone.

527
00:37:38,175 --> 00:37:40,135
Yeah, it totally upended me.

528
00:37:41,845 --> 00:37:44,681
I, uh... I started
suffering from blackouts.

529
00:37:44,765 --> 00:37:46,767
Charles.

530
00:37:46,767 --> 00:37:48,602
Morning, Charles.

531
00:37:49,186 --> 00:37:52,523
couldn't be with me
unless I got sober. So I did.

532
00:37:54,024 --> 00:37:55,859
But I did it more for my dad's memory.

533
00:37:55,943 --> 00:37:57,110
Charles?

534
00:37:58,904 --> 00:37:59,905
Charles?

535
00:38:08,997 --> 00:38:10,249
Charles.

536
00:38:14,127 --> 00:38:15,128
Charles.

537
00:38:16,964 --> 00:38:19,299
Charles.

538
00:38:19,925 --> 00:38:22,803
Catherine.

539
00:38:22,803 --> 00:38:25,055
Catherine. You haven't spoken.

540
00:38:27,182 --> 00:38:30,352
Um, my name's Catherine.
I'm an alcoholic.

541
00:38:30,352 --> 00:38:31,937
Hi, Catherine.

542
00:38:32,521 --> 00:38:34,064
I'll just listen tonight.

543
00:39:23,030 --> 00:39:24,698
You know you left the front door open?

544
00:39:24,698 --> 00:39:25,908
I saw you driving up.

545
00:39:26,575 --> 00:39:28,535
Are you sure you didn't
leave it open by mistake?

546
00:39:32,831 --> 00:39:34,166
I prepared a second piece.

547
00:39:39,546 --> 00:39:40,672
You can cook.

548
00:39:42,508 --> 00:39:44,760
Have you heard from
your mother recently?

549
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:45,844
Oh.

550
00:39:46,678 --> 00:39:50,140
Yeah. A postcard from
Istanbul of all places.

551
00:39:51,517 --> 00:39:54,728
She's opening a guesthouse
with her current boyfriend.

552
00:39:56,104 --> 00:39:57,814
And you're out of lemons.

553
00:39:57,898 --> 00:40:01,652
Yeah, well, that plan will have
changed by the time the card arrived.

554
00:40:01,652 --> 00:40:03,362
Yeah. Boyfriend too, knowing her.

555
00:40:04,321 --> 00:40:07,324
You know, I always
expected her to turn up here

556
00:40:07,324 --> 00:40:09,618
with a KGB spook on her arm.

557
00:40:11,286 --> 00:40:13,413
That would have been
the ultimate rebellion.

558
00:40:13,497 --> 00:40:14,998
No. This is... It's as
hard as an egg, this.

559
00:40:15,082 --> 00:40:16,500
You know they keep better in the fridge.

560
00:40:16,500 --> 00:40:19,086
I always understood a
lemon could last as long

561
00:40:19,086 --> 00:40:20,921
as an 18th century naval voyage.

562
00:40:20,921 --> 00:40:22,756
Yes. Well, this is the 21st century,

563
00:40:22,840 --> 00:40:26,176
so we can take full advantage of
modern food-preservation techniques.

564
00:40:26,260 --> 00:40:28,720
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Oh,
the chicken's burning.

565
00:40:29,388 --> 00:40:30,556
Shit.

566
00:40:30,556 --> 00:40:33,684
No, it's not bu... It's searing.
It's exactly the way I wanted it.

567
00:40:39,398 --> 00:40:41,567
Did you ever come across Robert Hobden?

568
00:40:42,651 --> 00:40:46,446
Ah. So you didn't visit
me just to lecture me

569
00:40:46,530 --> 00:40:49,157
on home safety and food hygiene.

570
00:40:49,241 --> 00:40:50,670
No, no. I wanted to see you too. I did.

571
00:40:50,671 --> 00:40:52,911
Not wanted to see me that much lately.

572
00:40:52,995 --> 00:40:56,170
Yeah. Well, not really been
that much to report, has there?

573
00:40:56,171 --> 00:40:57,171
From Slough House.

574
00:40:57,224 --> 00:40:59,293
They won't keep you there forever.

575
00:40:59,835 --> 00:41:02,129
I was given the impression
that they probably will.

576
00:41:02,129 --> 00:41:03,755
Well, that's the point.

577
00:41:03,839 --> 00:41:06,675
If you knew it was for only
six months, it wouldn't hurt.

578
00:41:06,675 --> 00:41:08,969
Yeah. It's been eight months.

579
00:41:08,969 --> 00:41:10,150
Well, you do your time.

580
00:41:10,151 --> 00:41:13,640
Whatever grunt work Jackson
Lamb throws your way.

581
00:41:13,724 --> 00:41:17,519
Then you head back to Regent's
Park. Your sins forgiven.

582
00:41:17,603 --> 00:41:20,147
Lamb's been there years, so they've
obviously never forgiven him.

583
00:41:20,147 --> 00:41:21,732
The man practically lives there.

584
00:41:21,732 --> 00:41:24,902
Was he ever actually good?
I just... I can't imagine it.

585
00:41:26,486 --> 00:41:27,487
I'll lay the table.

586
00:41:31,909 --> 00:41:35,996
You are not listening to me,
Jack. There is gonna be an attack.

587
00:41:35,996 --> 00:41:38,540
People are going to get hurt.

588
00:41:38,624 --> 00:41:41,335
I can't tell you any more
because I'll put myself at risk.

589
00:41:42,419 --> 00:41:45,839
No, no. Forget about any
fucking loyalty to me.

590
00:41:45,923 --> 00:41:47,758
Do this for your country.

591
00:41:51,470 --> 00:41:57,059
Fine. But know this. There
will be blood on your hands.

592
00:42:12,699 --> 00:42:14,660
You are coming tonight, aren't you?

593
00:42:14,660 --> 00:42:16,161
Of course I am.

594
00:42:16,245 --> 00:42:18,622
Good. 'Cause genuinely,
I might need backup.

595
00:42:18,622 --> 00:42:20,249
Have they started on you again?

596
00:42:20,832 --> 00:42:25,128
People are messaging the club
saying that they shouldn't book me.

597
00:42:25,212 --> 00:42:26,213
What?

598
00:42:26,213 --> 00:42:28,882
It's like you can't even
say the word "religion" now

599
00:42:28,966 --> 00:42:30,676
without somebody taking offense.

600
00:42:30,676 --> 00:42:33,220
- Yeah.
- My stuff isn't even that controversial.

601
00:42:33,220 --> 00:42:35,430
And the stuff that
is was written by you.

602
00:42:35,514 --> 00:42:36,849
Yeah.

603
00:42:38,016 --> 00:42:39,726
Are you sure you just
don't wanna get up there?

604
00:42:40,477 --> 00:42:44,857
Look, I will sit in the
audience and confuse everybody

605
00:42:44,857 --> 00:42:48,235
by laughing loudly each
time you mention Muslims.

606
00:42:58,328 --> 00:42:59,663
Here you go.

607
00:43:01,248 --> 00:43:02,374
Thank you.

608
00:43:02,374 --> 00:43:04,001
So, what happened to your hand?

609
00:43:05,127 --> 00:43:07,129
Oh. Nothing. I burned it on a grill.

610
00:43:08,046 --> 00:43:09,882
Was there a flashbox in the grill?

611
00:43:13,468 --> 00:43:15,971
All right. Yes, I tried to open
a flashbox without the code.

612
00:43:15,971 --> 00:43:18,223
Stupid thing to do.
Have you had it seen to?

613
00:43:18,307 --> 00:43:20,434
No, no. It's fine. It's
nothing to worry about.

614
00:43:23,312 --> 00:43:24,479
What was in the box?

615
00:43:27,107 --> 00:43:30,944
A laptop. With files
taken from Robert Hobden.

616
00:43:31,904 --> 00:43:33,405
Anyone know you pulled this stunt?

617
00:43:33,405 --> 00:43:36,325
- No. No.
- Good. Good. Keep it that way.

618
00:43:36,909 --> 00:43:37,951
Yes.

619
00:43:40,078 --> 00:43:41,496
It's just strange. It's just...

620
00:43:41,580 --> 00:43:44,708
It's not the usual crap they get
you to do there in Slough House.

621
00:43:44,708 --> 00:43:48,712
It's... I mean the Park are
on it. They're on Hobden.

622
00:43:48,712 --> 00:43:50,297
- Why?
- I don't know.

623
00:43:50,297 --> 00:43:53,133
- That's what I was trying to find out.
- Hmm.

624
00:43:54,009 --> 00:43:56,178
And I was hoping that
you could just tell me.

625
00:43:57,596 --> 00:44:00,140
Yeah, well, um...

626
00:44:01,892 --> 00:44:05,020
Hobden had had a run-in with MI5 before.

627
00:44:06,146 --> 00:44:08,023
He was a communist in his youth.

628
00:44:08,815 --> 00:44:13,987
Then he changed sides.
One-nation Tory, star columnist.

629
00:44:14,613 --> 00:44:17,074
Then the loathsome
drift to the far right.

630
00:44:17,074 --> 00:44:19,618
His career ended when his name appeared

631
00:44:19,618 --> 00:44:23,789
on a leaked list of donors to
the British Patriotic Party.

632
00:44:23,789 --> 00:44:27,251
Hobden always claimed that it
was MI5 that leaked the list.

633
00:44:28,168 --> 00:44:31,380
I can't comment, but if we
didn't do it, we should've done.

634
00:44:32,548 --> 00:44:36,051
Can't have fascists
hiding in plain sight.

635
00:44:36,802 --> 00:44:39,847
But, I mean, he's no one.
He's... The man's a has-been.

636
00:44:39,847 --> 00:44:41,765
I just don't understand why
they even bother looking at him.

637
00:44:41,849 --> 00:44:45,227
I've told you all I know,
and you should stay out of it.

638
00:44:45,227 --> 00:44:48,063
And if the Park are looking at
him, there'll be a good reason.

639
00:44:48,856 --> 00:44:50,941
And if they're using
Slough House to do it,

640
00:44:50,941 --> 00:44:52,943
it means they don't want blowback.

641
00:44:54,027 --> 00:44:56,071
Which puts you at risk.

642
00:44:59,116 --> 00:45:00,242
You understand?

643
00:45:02,452 --> 00:45:03,996
And remember... hmm?

644
00:45:06,582 --> 00:45:09,918
Moscow rules, watch your back.
London rules, cover your arse.

645
00:45:10,002 --> 00:45:11,503
- Yeah.
- Very good.

646
00:45:13,005 --> 00:45:16,133
How come every picture of Jesus

647
00:45:16,133 --> 00:45:18,802
has him looking like a
millennial gap year student?

648
00:45:20,053 --> 00:45:21,513
He... He's got everything, right?

649
00:45:21,597 --> 00:45:25,809
He's got the likes of hipster,
long hair, the beard, the sandals.

650
00:45:25,893 --> 00:45:27,644
He looks like a sort of 35-year-old man

651
00:45:27,728 --> 00:45:29,855
who still thinks the
band is gonna make it big.

652
00:45:32,524 --> 00:45:36,361
So... Jesus, Buddha and
Allah walk into a pub.

653
00:45:36,445 --> 00:45:37,446
Oh, no.

654
00:45:38,864 --> 00:45:41,491
And the mood goes like that.

655
00:45:42,451 --> 00:45:43,535
Like this actually.

656
00:45:45,162 --> 00:45:49,082
And they... they go to
the bar. They order drinks.

657
00:45:50,250 --> 00:45:51,885
Tap water for Jesus 'cause,

658
00:45:51,886 --> 00:45:54,254
you know, he can turn
that into wine for free.

659
00:45:54,838 --> 00:45:57,925
Diet Coke for Buddha because he's,
uh... he's watching his weight.

660
00:45:57,925 --> 00:46:01,136
And, uh, alcohol-free beer for Allah.

661
00:46:02,346 --> 00:46:04,806
- Nah, I'm done with this.
- And, uh, I'll... Really?

662
00:46:04,890 --> 00:46:06,644
Don't worry about
them, guys. Don't worry.

663
00:46:06,645 --> 00:46:08,519
Just, uh... Just treat them like an STD.

664
00:46:08,519 --> 00:46:10,604
If you ignore them,
they'll probably go away.

665
00:46:12,356 --> 00:46:16,360
And let me tell you,
they had a lovely time.

666
00:46:16,360 --> 00:46:18,987
They really did. Honestly,
they stayed out all night.

667
00:46:19,071 --> 00:46:21,448
Jesus got crucified and
wasn't seen for three days.

668
00:46:23,742 --> 00:46:26,828
I don't know why you guys were
worr... Why were you worried?

669
00:46:28,539 --> 00:46:31,792
Absolutely killed it tonight. That
was the best I've ever seen you.

670
00:46:32,543 --> 00:46:33,544
Hey, you were great.

671
00:46:33,544 --> 00:46:34,670
Oh, thank you.

672
00:46:34,670 --> 00:46:36,797
Hey, you were great.

673
00:46:36,797 --> 00:46:38,298
And you were so relaxed as well.

674
00:46:38,382 --> 00:46:39,750
Strongest material, though,

675
00:46:39,751 --> 00:46:42,052
is your "Jesus, Buddha
and Allah walk into a pub."

676
00:46:42,052 --> 00:46:43,929
You need to get up there.

677
00:46:45,264 --> 00:46:47,516
So you, uh, head-in for
the nine o'clock tomorrow?

678
00:46:48,267 --> 00:46:49,518
You gonna be in?

679
00:46:49,518 --> 00:46:50,811
Nine o'clock. Nope. No.

680
00:46:51,478 --> 00:46:53,063
- No way.
- All right, mate.

681
00:46:53,063 --> 00:46:54,439
I'll see you in the week, yeah?

682
00:46:54,523 --> 00:46:56,441
Okay. Take care, bro. Thank you so much.

683
00:46:57,150 --> 00:46:58,944
- You killed it.
- Killer work.

684
00:47:16,587 --> 00:47:20,007
Wait! Oi! Hey!

685
00:47:20,007 --> 00:47:22,676
No! No! No, no, no! No!

686
00:47:22,676 --> 00:47:27,181
Help! Help me!

687
00:48:09,097 --> 00:48:12,684
Roddy, can you...
check something for me?

688
00:48:12,768 --> 00:48:16,021
Not on the clock yet. You'll
need to pay my private rate.

689
00:48:16,021 --> 00:48:18,148
Yep.

690
00:48:27,074 --> 00:48:29,201
Just tell what it is
I'm looking at on there.

691
00:48:32,371 --> 00:48:34,081
- Don't touch that!
- All right.

692
00:48:42,381 --> 00:48:43,382
It's pi.

693
00:48:44,883 --> 00:48:46,593
- Is that a code?
- No. It's pi.

694
00:48:46,677 --> 00:48:48,679
Running to an infinite number of places.

695
00:48:48,679 --> 00:48:49,860
Is there anything else behind it?

696
00:48:49,861 --> 00:48:51,473
Any other files on the stick? Anything?

697
00:48:51,557 --> 00:48:52,724
No. Where'd you get it?

698
00:48:52,808 --> 00:48:53,809
Hobden.

699
00:48:56,061 --> 00:48:57,479
You copied the files.

700
00:48:57,980 --> 00:48:59,731
You'd only know that if
you'd looked at it yourself.

701
00:48:59,815 --> 00:49:01,650
Well, at least I didn't
need Ho to tell me it was pi.

702
00:49:01,650 --> 00:49:04,486
Everybody needs me.
They just don't know it.

703
00:49:05,028 --> 00:49:06,572
Seems like he used it as a decoy.

704
00:49:06,572 --> 00:49:09,533
He was expecting a snatch. Cool cat.

705
00:49:10,284 --> 00:49:12,536
Thanks, Roddy. Very helpful.

706
00:49:14,872 --> 00:49:16,832
Why would he be expecting a snatch?

707
00:49:16,832 --> 00:49:18,790
I don't know. What do
you think the Park will do

708
00:49:18,791 --> 00:49:20,669
if they find out you opened a flashbox?

709
00:49:20,669 --> 00:49:22,880
Yeah, well, they're not
gonna find out, are they?

710
00:49:26,425 --> 00:49:27,467
Did it hurt?

711
00:49:27,551 --> 00:49:30,095
No. Well, a bit.

712
00:49:31,805 --> 00:49:33,640
Fuck! Jesus Christ, Sid.

713
00:49:33,724 --> 00:49:35,434
Look, I know you landed
here with a bump...

714
00:49:35,434 --> 00:49:38,187
- Yeah. I've still got whiplash.
- If you want to do something useful,

715
00:49:38,187 --> 00:49:40,314
you can get rid of the stinking
rubbish that's still in our office.

716
00:49:40,314 --> 00:49:43,192
Yeah, but I wanna actually be
properly useful, Sid. Don't you?

717
00:49:43,192 --> 00:49:45,800
Do something. I mean, it...

718
00:49:45,801 --> 00:49:48,071
I could not be more
bored if I tried, Sid.

719
00:49:48,155 --> 00:49:49,907
And I have actually tried.

720
00:49:49,907 --> 00:49:51,533
And if the Park are looking at Hobden,

721
00:49:51,617 --> 00:49:54,912
then that means there is
something finally happening here.

722
00:49:54,912 --> 00:49:57,080
Exactly. It's the Park's
business, not ours.

723
00:49:57,497 --> 00:49:59,499
Cartwright, come see this!

724
00:50:07,925 --> 00:50:09,551
- Following a breaking story...
- Hostage.

725
00:50:13,972 --> 00:50:15,015
Is it live?

726
00:50:15,015 --> 00:50:17,434
Popped up on a Middle East
chat feed a few hours ago.

727
00:50:17,518 --> 00:50:19,269
Media have just picked up on it.

728
00:50:19,353 --> 00:50:20,979
He's holding today's Express.

729
00:50:22,314 --> 00:50:23,899
Shit. He's being held here.

730
00:50:23,899 --> 00:50:27,277
What appears to be here
in the heart of Britain.

731
00:50:27,361 --> 00:50:28,980
recording first surfaced

732
00:50:28,981 --> 00:50:30,948
this morning on social media...

733
00:50:30,948 --> 00:50:33,534
What we really need now is leadership.

734
00:50:33,534 --> 00:50:36,328
Who's collating lists on
recently active groups?

735
00:50:36,328 --> 00:50:37,538
I am, ma'am.

736
00:50:37,538 --> 00:50:39,164
I wanted a breakdown of
that a half an hour ago.

737
00:50:39,248 --> 00:50:41,041
- Yes, ma'am.
